      "components": ["U4", "C11"],
      "pins": ["U4.27", "C11.1"],
      "nets": ["VCC"],
      "observed": "U4 pin 27 (VCOMH) and C11 pin 1 are both on the VCC net. The netlist's VCC net includes (node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"27\") (pinfunction \"VCOMH\") (pintype \"output\")) and (node (ref \"C11\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")).",
      "expected": "VCOMH should be a separate net connected only to C11 (and not to VCC), as the SSD1306 charge-pump output with its reservoir capacitor to GND.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "C11 (4.7 µF) — U4 VCOMH (charge-pump output) to GND, the output reservoir/filter cap"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"27\") (pinfunction \"VCOMH\") (pintype \"output\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"C11\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The SSD1306 charge-pump output (which can be a high voltage) is shorted to the 3.3V VCC rail, likely causing excessive current, damaging the SSD1306, MCU, or other components, and preventing proper display operation.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain one clear anomaly: the SSD1306 VCOMH charge-pump output is tied to the VCC supply rail instead of being a separate net with C11 to GND, as the specification requires."
}

